## What the charge is

A missed appointment, under the Calloway Limited Home Warranty, is a booked repair or inspection appointment at which the homeowner did not provide access. The missed-appointment charge is the homeowner charge such a missed appointment carries on the homeowner's coverage. It is worked out on the day it is assessed and it is linked to the claim item of the missed appointment. Once booked, it appears with its own charge number on the homeowner's warranty invoice and in the coverage's charge history, and its amount is added to the warranty charges the homeowner owes on that coverage.

## Booking the charge

Tool: `assess_missed_appointment_charge_27486c7f`, an agent-side tool. The desk agent unlocks it and then calls it; the homeowner does not run it. One call books one missed-appointment charge, dated the day of the call.

| Parameter | What it is | Format |
|---|---|---|
| `coverage_id` | The reference number of the homeowner's warranty coverage on the home, as returned by the warranty coverage lookup for this homeowner | Identifier, as returned by the lookup |
| `claim_item_ref` | The service request item number of the claim item whose appointment was missed | Copied character for character, digits and hyphens included, exactly as printed on the homeowner's service request and shown in the coverage's warranty history, with no reformatting |
| `amount` | The charge amount in US dollars | A positive number with 2 decimal places, already rounded to the nearest cent; no currency sign or thousands separator |

## What the call returns

A receipt whose `status` is `charge_booked` means the charge is on the coverage. The receipt also gives:

- `warranty_event_id` — reference number of the new charge entry;
- `charge_reference` — the charge number printed on the homeowner invoice, text such as WCH-51234;
- `coverage_id` — the coverage charged;
- `claim_item_ref` — the item the charge is linked to;
- `charge_type` — always `missed_appointment_fee`;
- `amount` — in US dollars, 2 decimal places;
- `event_date` — the assessment date, in the form YYYY-MM-DD;
- `charges_due` — the homeowner's warranty charges owed on the coverage including this charge, in US dollars, 2 decimal places.

**Illustrative call (hypothetical values).** `coverage_id` WC-000123, `claim_item_ref` WSR-20417-03, `amount` 75.00 returns `status` `charge_booked`, a new `charge_reference`, `charge_type` `missed_appointment_fee` and `charges_due` raised by 75.00.
